A unit test can call new OrderService(fakeRepository). No Spring context and no reflection utility is required. With one constructor, Spring selects it without @Autowired. This style does not magically make all state immutable, nor does it mean every optional extension belongs in the constructor. Use a setter or provider only when absence or late resolution is part of the real design.

