Optional injection needs an explicit fallback.

~~~java
@Component
class ReportService {
    private final ObjectProvider<AuditSink> auditSink;

    ReportService(ObjectProvider<AuditSink> auditSink) {
        this.auditSink = auditSink;
    }

    void generate() {
        auditSink.ifAvailable(sink -> sink.record("report"));
    }
}
~~~

A setter can express the same optional relationship, but code must still handle the missing value. If ReportService cannot meet its contract without AuditSink, the dependency is not optional and belongs in the constructor.

